  "body": "## What changed\n\n- Added `Warning::StockChamferGouge { at: usize }` to `crates/sim/src/verify/types.rs`.\n- Its `Display` text reads: `move {at} cuts past the finish surface (stock-source chamfer breaks into a part; chamfer with the part as source)`.\n- Added `operation::keep_law::note_stock_chamfer_gouges` in `crates/app/src/operation/keep_law.rs`.\n- Called `note_stock_chamfer_gouges` after kept-part solid-law checks in `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs` (both aligned and tilted arms) and `crates/app/src/operation/kept_rejudge.rs`.\n- Mapped `Warning::StockChamferGouge` to `\"gouge\"` in `crates/app/src/mcp/job.rs`, to move `at` in `crates/app/src/warned_moves.rs`, and to its own fold key in `crates/ui/src/operations.rs`.\n- Updated `gouges()` in `crates/app/tests/stock_source_holes_support/mod.rs` and added a pinning test in `crates/app/tests/stock_source_holes.rs`.\n- Recorded the design decision in `docs/decisions/1637-stock-chamfer-part-source-hint.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nAfter PR #1634, a stock-source 2D Chamfer flush with a part emits `Warning::Gouge` from `contain_into` (`DepthLaw::Keep`) against the kept parts.\n`GenerateOperation`, `posting::post_setup`, `mcp::job::verify`, and the UI warning fold all read `tp.warnings`, not `tp.path.notes`.\nBecause `Warning::Gouge` carries no operation context, callers saw `move N cuts past the finish surface` with no cause or workaround.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Pinning test: `stock_source_chamfer_refusal_names_cause_and_part_as_source_workaround` in `crates/app/tests/stock_source_holes.rs` failed before the fix (saw only `move 1 cuts past the finish surface`) and passed after the fix across generate, post, live `kept_rejudge`, part-source verification, and MCP `verify`.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test stock_source_holes`: 8 passed, 0 failed.\n- Mutation 1: temporarily reverted `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs` to `upstream/main`; `stock_source_chamfer_refusal_names_cause_and_part_as_source_workaround` failed as expected, then passed after restoring the fix.\n- Mutation 2: temporarily reverted `crates/app/src/operation/kept_rejudge.rs` to `upstream/main`; `stock_source_chamfer_refusal_names_cause_and_part_as_source_workaround` failed on `chamfer-rejudge-hint`, then passed after restoring the fix.\n- `cargo run --manifest-path xtask/Cargo.toml -- gate quick --base upstream/main`: `sim suites` passed (49s), `motion suites` passed (8s), `ui suites` passed (250s); `app suites` passed all suites except the pre-existing failure on `upstream/main` `0db66c44` (`crates/app/tests/winding_align.rs :: the_inside_out_stl_fixture_reads_inside_out_and_refuses`, tracked in #1752 / PR #1761).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed with 0 warnings.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Direct interactive egui rendering of `fold_warnings_located` for `StockChamferGouge` beyond UI unit/test suite compilation and `ui suites` passing.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- Touches `crates/app/src/mcp/job.rs` alongside #1699 and #1738 in different functions (`finding` vs `get_job` and `setups_view`); whichever merges second refreshes.\n- Touches `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs` alongside #1713 in different functions (`DepthLaw::Keep` kept-parts check vs `Finish3D` / 5-axis); whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: Name the part-collision cause and the `chamfer with the part as source` workaround when a stock-source 2D Chamfer breaks into a part.\n\nFixes #1637\n",
